# Pinned external conformance tests (M1 slice 3; corpus/conformance.py).
# Fetched, never committed — like the corpus in MANIFEST.toml. One line per
# file: <sha256>  <suite>  <url>, every url at a fixed commit.
#
#   w3c  The W3C OWL 2 conformance suite (the OWL Working Group's test cases,
#        W3C licence), as HermiT carries it: all.rdf at owlcs/hermit-reasoner
#        65d38905. The WG approved these results; no reasoner produced them.
#   elk  ELK's classification tests (Apache-2.0): each input .owl with the
#        .taxonomy ELK's authors expect, liveontologies/elk-reasoner cc556787,
#        elk-reasoner/src/test/resources/test_input/classification/.
#   elk-entailment  ELK's entailment queries at the same commit: an input with
#        the axioms it must (.entailed) and must not (.notentailed) entail,
#        elk-reasoner/src/test/resources/test_input/query/entailment/.
#
# To re-pin: change the commit in every url, recompute each sha256, and review
# the resulting change to corpus/conformance-status.txt.
